To find the points of inflection, we solve ${f}^{″}(x)=0.$ This gives\n\n$$\n-6x-6=0\\,⟹\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we need to check that the concavity changes at $x=-1.$ To do that, we take two points, one to the left of $x=-1$ and another to the right of $x=-1.$ \n\nFor example, let's take the points $x=-2$ and $x=0.$ We compute the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the selected points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-2) & =-6(-2)-6=6>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =-6(0)-6=-6<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second derivative changes sign at $x=-1.$ \n\nSince the concavity changes at $x=-1,$ we conclude that $x=-1$ is indeed a point of inflection." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042687/state.json" "file_sha256" "a6f1d170e5a48ef81274ae586a7f78a7b3db9b5f3294e2c081b4dede1ce9ba71"} {"question" "q-128289" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "176a1d1670dc87fc78fcfbd8eed27dca686dccf8374febd805c64d96e5b227bf"} {"question" "q-128289" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042687/state.json" "file_sha256" "a6f1d170e5a48ef81274ae586a7f78a7b3db9b5f3294e2c081b4dede1ce9ba71"} {"question" "q-128289" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042687/state.json" "file_sha256" "a6f1d170e5a48ef81274ae586a7f78a7b3db9b5f3294e2c081b4dede1ce9ba71"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1566 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
